    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d96">

                <pb facs="0199" n="103" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg103"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867n.6363/23</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wheeler</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-12-30"><hi rendition="#italic">December 30,
                        1921</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received January 12, 1922.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 824</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the Embassy’s telegram No.
                    978, of December 15, 4 p.m.,<anchor n="50" xml:id="d96-f1"/> and its despatch
                    No. 724, of December 1, regarding the desire of the Standard Oil Company to
                    continue geological examinations in certain areas of Palestine, I have the honor
                    to transmit herewith copies (in triplicate) of a further note received from the
                    Foreign Office upon this subject, dated December 28, 1921. This Note, as will be
                    noted in paragraph four, was sent without waiting <pb facs="0200" n="104"
                        xml:id="pg104"/> for the results of the further enquiries addressed to the
                    Palestine Government, reference to which is made in the telegram above
                    mentioned.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Post Wheeler</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d96-a1.xml" xpointer="d96-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
